          "en": "our images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.59,
          "end": 18.28,
          "en": "We are rendering a couple of images here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.28,
          "end": 20.66,
          "en": "when we rendered that list of events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.66,
          "end": 23.55,
          "en": "And also when we explore a single event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.55,
          "end": 25.53,
          "en": "here we also have an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.53,
          "end": 30.23,
          "en": "And in both cases, those images are not optimized at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.23,
          "end": 32.05,
          "en": "Let me show you what that means.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.05,
          "end": 34.02,
          "en": "On the All Events page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.02,
          "end": 35.95,
          "en": "if I open the developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.95,
          "end": 38.77,
          "en": "and we go to the Network tab here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.77,
          "end": 41.96,
          "en": "If we then empty the cache and hard reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.96,
          "end": 44.38,
          "en": "by right clicking on the refresh icon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.38,
          "end": 47.65,
          "en": "we make sure that we reload all the data for this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 47.65,
          "end": 49.77,
          "en": "including the images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.77,
          "end": 53.44,
          "en": "And now let's have a look at this coding-event.jpg file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.44,
          "end": 55,
          "en": "If I make this a bit bigger,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55,
          "end": 58.37,
          "en": "we see that this image has two megabytes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.37,
          "end": 60.97,
          "en": "The introvert and extrovert images are even worse,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.97,
          "end": 63.27,
          "en": "they have five and four megabytes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.27,
          "end": 65.25,
          "en": "The reason for this is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.25,
          "end": 68.41,
          "en": "these are huge unoptimized images,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.41,
          "end": 72.22,
          "en": "which are fetched in full size and quality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.22,
          "end": 76.85,
          "en": "And we are also always using the same image type, jpeg,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.85,
          "end": 81.26,
          "en": "no matter if our browser maybe supports a better type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.26,
          "end": 86.26,
          "en": "For example, Chrome would support the webp image type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.3,
          "end": 89.06,
          "en": "which is an optimized image format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.06,
          "end": 91.92,
          "en": "Now for development, that's no problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.92,
          "end": 94.61,
          "en": "but this would not be okay for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.61,
          "end": 97.43,
          "en": "These would be way too big images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.43,
          "end": 99.75,
          "en": "And Next.js calls itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.75,
          "end": 102.87,
          "en": "the react framework for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.87,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "And shipping such big images is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 106.63,
          "en": "certainly not production ready.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.63,
          "end": 108.85,
          "en": "Therefore, for it makes a lot of sense that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.85,
          "end": 112.15,
          "en": "Next.js also helps us with images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.15,
          "end": 114.81,
          "en": "It helps us optimize those images,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 117.973,
          "en": "and it does so in a super simple way.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
